# The for-of steps by protocol, so the counted loop stands under the handler that closes the iterator. That handler reads nothing of the loop.
# The loop's own text subtracts what it reads off its records, so its turns may begin again under such a handler, and looks may count on that, as they do where the outer loop goes by index.
# Two doors had to open together: the turns alone, or the looks alone, left every read of a field to a stub: four times the instructions.
# With the typed turns the counter of the loop is a known induction; under a handler that shuts them none is.
# STATISTIC: KnownInductionsUsed >= 1
# RUN: compile mechanisms=all
# CHECK: image not empty
